{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Because that Abraham hearkened, etc.</b> The verse has י\"ד words corresponding to the י\"ד commandments in which there are עק\"ב words, and corresponding to them he was tested with י\"ד trials and sustained the world that was created with י' utterances: עק\"ב — two: \"he hearkened to My voice\"; third: recognized his Creator; and his years קע\"ה:" "<b>Because that Abraham hearkened</b> — in gematria: קיים עירובי תבשילין (he established eruv tavshilin). And there was added for him an extra ה to his name corresponding to \"My voice, My charge, My commandments, My statutes, and My teachings.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase 'in which there are עק\"ב words' likely refers to the Ten Commandments themselves containing 172 words; the subsequent list 'two… third…' appears to enumerate Abraham's recognitions or actions, but the sequence is terse and possibly truncated."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:03.493398977Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}